-- Migration version 6 → 7: stale-event guard on the `nostr_profiles`
-- cache.
--
-- Pre-fix the upsert was `INSERT OR REPLACE`, which blindly overwrote
-- the cache row regardless of which Kind-0 event was the freshest.
-- Combined with `firstOrNull()` in `fetchProfileFromRelays`, a
-- mis-configured or hostile relay that races to deliver an older
-- Kind-0 first could pin the user's cached `lud16` to a stale
-- (potentially attacker-controlled) lightning address — zaps would
-- then route to that wallet until the next cache eviction (which
-- doesn't happen on its own).
--
-- The new column persists `event.createdAt` (Unix seconds) of the
-- Kind-0 the row was built from. The upsert query (`upsert` in
-- `NostrProfiles.sq`) becomes `INSERT … ON CONFLICT … WHERE excluded
-- .last_event_created_at > IFNULL(existing.last_event_created_at, 0)`
-- so older events are silently rejected. Mirrors the stale-event
-- guard already in place for `climbs` (Board.sq getClimbCreatedAt /
-- isExistingNewer in CommunityClimbSubscriber).
--
-- Existing rows get NULL for the new column; the IFNULL(0) clause in
-- the upsert query treats them as "freshness unknown" and lets any
-- subsequent Kind-0 event populate the field.

ALTER TABLE nostr_profiles ADD COLUMN last_event_created_at INTEGER;
